# Local deploy + offline-live-KV secrets. Copy to .env.deploy and fill in — NEVER commit.
# This file is where THIS checkout learns which instance it belongs to: the engine names
# no account, project, worker or shell repo anywhere in its source.
#
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN: Pages deploy + KV read/write token (Cloudflare dashboard).
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID: the Cloudflare account id.
# GV_KV_NS: the KV namespace id the worker's overlay data lives in.
# PAGES_PROJECT: the Cloudflare Pages project `npm run deploy` ships to.
# GV_IDENTITY_PATH / GV_DEPLOY_CONFIG_PATH: paths to your deploy shell's identity.json
#   and deploy.config.json (the shell is a sibling clone; its repo name is yours to pick).
#   `npm run deploy` requires both — without them a build has no user list and would ship
#   an ungated site. Offline mode auto-detects them, so it needs neither.
# REALTIME_CONFIG: path to your shell's realtime.wrangler.toml, for `npm run
#   deploy:realtime` (canvas multiplayer). See realtime/wrangler.example.toml.
# RT_SHARED_SECRET: the same shared secret your deployed workers hold — offline mode
#   passes it to the local worker so canvas boards can join the instance's real rooms.
#   Without it (but with live KV) the realtime worker refuses the join and offline
#   boards silently run solo. Leave unset if your realtime worker has no secret.
# REVIEW_SITE_URL / REVIEW_EXPORT_KEY: `npm run review` — read/moderate comment threads.
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=
GV_KV_NS=
PAGES_PROJECT=
GV_IDENTITY_PATH=../your-deploy-shell/identity.json
GV_DEPLOY_CONFIG_PATH=../your-deploy-shell/deploy.config.json
REALTIME_CONFIG=../your-deploy-shell/realtime.wrangler.toml
RT_SHARED_SECRET=
REVIEW_SITE_URL=https://your-project.pages.dev
REVIEW_EXPORT_KEY=
